\pard\plain \li950\ri1757\sa160\sl259\slmult1\ql\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The airlock status indicator eased down from the active status as the internal pressure matched that of the Balaenoptera\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s halls. John checked the recruits packing up on the range from the live feed in the airlock, disconnected his helmet and placed it in an automated mag lev pod that would soon return his suit to the tech service bay where it would then find its way to John\u8217\'92s designated jump bay location alongside his team\u8217\'92s. He took a deep breath, sighed, then opened the airlock.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 As the airlock doors opened, a light fog bellowed out from the airlock into the Balaenoptera\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s main transit hall. The cold air of the airlock clashed with the more human-friendly temperature of the hall.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Standing gracefully before him, a tall yet frail figure waited patiently. A smirk across her weathered face, the lady stepped to the side, presenting her palm to John as he stepped out of the airlock.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Captain Walker,\u8221\'94 Lady Ava said gently. John raised his hand to meet hers with a gentle clasp. John stepped out from the airlock, his eyes meeting hers with a brief respectful gaze, complimented with a soft smile.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Lady Ava, what calls for concern? As much as I do enjoy our talks, we\u8217\'92ve been short-strawed another one of Marcellus\u8217\'92s secret missions early morning.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The pair walked back down the halls of the protectant flagship to John\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s quarters as they exchanged small talk in the open yet surprisingly empty halls.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I see they still have you on regular recruit training duties,\u8221\'94 John seemed un-phased by this remark.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s a welcome change of pace from the usual peacekeeping deployments, I can tell you that much.\u8221\'94 There was a slight annoyance in John\u8217\'92s tone, like he knew she was about to part some side objective on him.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Do you know anything about the new security clearance they\u8217\'92ve placed on accessing the asteroid interceptors\u8217\'92 firing logs? We tried to check them out earlier while we were waiting for the recruits. It seems all access has been recently barred.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You know yourself, John, even with my political sway, the reach of my birds on this ship has always had some limits, but that\u8217\'92s not to say I can\u8217\'92t go digging.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Let\u8217\'92s wait till we are at my quarters before going into too much detail. We don\u8217\'92t know who could be eavesdropping.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Cautious as always, why has it got you so riled up?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I thought transparency was something that was a guarantee when you operate at our level.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 John had a hint of disappointment in his tone.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 As he arrived at his door, he scanned his wrist while looking into the retinal scanner. A swift series of beeps confirmed his presence. His door swiftly opened, and he entered, then started removing items, packing down for bed. His room was pristine and organised, with few personal items to be seen other than a few photos of close family.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Ava paced over to the window in John\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s cabin, looking out over the remaining cadets collecting themselves on the hull having completed the training session. She couldn\u8217\'92t hear the footsteps, but she could see them growing tiresome. She was too, she thought to herself. It was late, and she wanted to ease John\u8217\'92s mind so she could return to her cell herself. Politics of an ever-expanding front, while keeping the Protectant in check, laid heavy upon her, and John could see it vaguely when she finished talking.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I see your concern, although, John,\u8221\'94 said Ava. She paused for a moment, taking time to recall the past in her weary state, then continued.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You know the designs of the turrets are not far dissimilar from those used in the previous war. Rail rifle technology\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 Japan always had a knack for producing the finest rail technology. The first to click onto it, actually. You ever wonder why Tau is so good at what she does?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Lady Meera paused, awaiting John\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s response.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I always took her for the Engineer when I first met her,\u8221\'94 said John.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Well,\u8221\'94 said Ava, \u8220\'93at this point, you might as well say the Protectant had met a plateau in their engineering prowess. Modularity, robustness\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 it had been engineered in as a staple of the Solar expansion. Waste was merely something of the past.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 She paced over to John\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s study, where he had portraits of his family laid out on his wall.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Aaah yes, she was a beauty\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 your mother, that photo. When was it taken, do you know?\u8221\'94 Ava gleaned in closer to the portrait. She could see a young happy boy, his dad\u8217\'92s hand resting on his shoulder.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Not sure,\u8221\'94 said John. \u8220\'93{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "scrivcmt://E2285C5C-E4C6-4709-A88B-8614834D8E4D"}{\fldrsltTowards the end of the 21st century, I think.}}\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Over half a century ago. I tend to lose track of time so easily... with the resleeving process and all.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What sleeve number are you on now?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93All original, believe it or not\u8230\'85 I could never get behind the whole feeling of being in a young body again. I believe, as a political figure, despite how many parties have used it to rally against me, being old... not with the times. Hell, my mind retains my experience, the body shows it in lessons learned on the skin.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s paid off though, it seems, Lady Ava,\u8221\'94 said John.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Ava humbly replied, \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Well... I still have a few tricks up my sleeves, John Walker, don\u8217\'92t you worry about that...\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 John was enjoying Lady Ava\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s company a little more now. He felt at home in a sense with her, and he couldn\u8217\'92t tell exactly why for a moment.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I knew your mother personally. She was a great woman.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I haven\u8217\'92t heard from her since the worker bot program was decommissioned.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Are you not at all curious as to why?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93My mother never really had much to do with me since I left for Protectant training. Don\u8217\'92t think she really approved of my choices. I was 17, fresh out of college.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Now now, I am sure that wasn\u8217\'92t the case. She probably just got caught up in her work more than anything.\u8221\'94 Ava was kind in her tone; you could tell she thought highly of John\u8217\'92s mother.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93She would be proud to see how far you\u8217\'92ve come.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 John didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t know exactly how to feel. He was silent for a moment.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I don\u8217\'92t remember much of my mother. I recall in my junior years before I turned 13, I would often be on the farm riding my race horse Beverly.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Oh yes, I recall. She had a thing for velocity, your mother.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 John paused for a minute. He seemed surprised.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You... you worked with mother?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93In my younger days, yes. We were quite the team, me and your mother, you know.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I didn\u8217\'92t realise you had a knack for technology.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Welll.. It wasn\u8217\'92t entirely technical the role, I was more in the political side of sorts\u8221\'94,\u8221\'94I See\u8221\'94, \u8220\'93Don\u8217\'92t worry, it didn\u8217\'92t stop me from having to get my hands dirty don\u8217\'92t you worry about that\u8221\'94. John layed down on his bunk, the navy blue mattress as rigid as it was, and routine in it\u8217\'92s aesthetic, John couldn\u8217\'92t help but feel it didn\u8217\'92t entirely feel like home, as familiar the bulkhead was to hi. Lady Ava glanced over at the seat beside the Hull window. \u8220\'93Actually, she made a shit storm for me your mother\u8221\'94 Lady Meera chuckled as she paced back to the port window. \u8220\'93It seems like such an age ago, I can only wonder what she is up to now\u8221\'94, \u8220\'93Like I said, haven\u8217\'92t heard from her since I left for protectant training\u8221\'94, \u8220\'93I have a strange feeling that her works are still very present in the universe, even after her project was decommissioned\u8221\'94, \u8220\'93Project?\u8221\'94 John pondered what on earth she could be talking about. \u8220\'93The Serva Vitae Project.. She had high hopes your mother, much like your father I believe, probably why they gravitated to one another. It\u8217\'92s no surprise really, with radical advancement, it seems there is always some radical response by the current algorithm, Technocrats couldn\u8217\'92t keep up if you ask me\u8221\'94 \u8220\'93People are afraid of what they don\u8217\'92t understand\u8221\'94 Said John \u8220\'93You should see the way the new recruits looked at us when we said we were jettisoning them off the ship and another person would be commandeering their suits\u8221\'94 \u8220\'93Well, I can assure you John, nothing scared your mother, not even losing her job it seems\u8221\'94, \u8220\'93Sounds like her, we once had a horse break out of it\u8217\'92s pen, thing was rabbid, she just stood there and stared it straight in the eyes, I didn\u8217\'92t think she was breathing\u8230\'85\u8221\'94 \u8220\'93Let me guess.. \u8221\'94 Said Ava. \u8220\'93The horse walked back into it\u8217\'92s pen\u8221\'94. \u8220\'93How did you know?\u8221\'94, \u8220\'93Oh I know the look she gave the horse, infact the look she gave your friend Marcellus\u8221\'94 \u8220\'93I see.. \u8221\'94 Said John. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93How did he handle that?\u8221\'94 \u8220\'93Funnily enough it worked\u8230\'85 of course until the horse realised she wasn\u8217\'92t bluffing\u8221\'94 \u8220\'93Bluffing?\u8221\'94 \u8220\'93Lets just say your mother was hard to contain in her work, a wildcard. She paid dearly for it. It was the back chatter around then\u8230\'85 I like to think she quietly slipped out the back door between me and you.. John\u8221\'94 John turned his head to make eye contact with Ava, she let out a slight smirk, like she was up to something. But he couldn\u8217\'92t put his finger on it.  }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Yes those were the old days we had only just broken the 3rd quarter of the 21st century. The economy struggled initially for a short while with the onset and testing of the new economy caused some minor conflicts on small fronts contained by the rapidly developing protectant and it\u8217\'92s rapidly expanding empire some might say. Then you had the Technocrats that justified the fluctuations had to be accounted for but the economy that tried to keep up. The Federation collectively had focused resources on Exploration, and in doing so solved several shortfalls along the way.. But lets not get carried away with economy, It seems they can\u8217\'92t afford to be releasing the vector data of those Asteroid interceptors to a new threat!\u8221\'94 Ava paused for a moment. \u8220\'93Whatever you do down there John tomorrow, be careful.. I have a feeling that we are being watched,\u8221\'94 \u8220\'93you think there\u8217\'92s an insider?\u8221\'94 \u8220\'93Not in your immediate squad\u8221\'94 Meera\u8217\'92s eyes fixed softly with johns \u8220\'93But I needn\u8217\'92t think you should worry about it\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 John sat quietly for a moment, absorbing Ava\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s words. The soft hum of the ship's systems played in the background, faint vibrations running through the floor like a heartbeat\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 steady, controlled, but ever-present.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He looked out through the other observation port, his gaze drawn to the distant asteroid fields glinting faintly against the void. The protectant, the Federation, the economy\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 words that used to mean something tangible now seemed like faint echoes of a world long past. Out here, in the dark, the only currency that mattered was trust, and even that felt thinly stretched.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You think they\u8217\'92re tracking us already?\u8221\'94 John asked, breaking the silence. His voice was calm, measured, but the slight crease in his brow betrayed his unease.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Lady Meera tilted her head, her expression unreadable as she leaned against the bulkhead. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Tracking? No,\u8221\'94 she said softly. \u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s not that simple. Surveillance isn\u8217\'92t just about sensors or signals anymore. It\u8217\'92s about patterns. Behaviors. Movements. A system designed to predict, not just observe.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 John's fingers drummed lightly on the edge of the console. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re talking about behavioral algorithms, aren\u8217\'92t you?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Ava nodded. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Exactly. They don\u8217\'92t need a direct line on you when they can predict where you\u8217\'92ll be, what you\u8217\'92ll do. And those asteroid interceptors... if the data leaks, it\u8217\'92s not just about one mission. It\u8217\'92s the whole defense network. Vulnerable.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Ava, who had been silent till now, finally spoke, her voice carrying a note of sarcasm to cut through the tension. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Well, let\u8217\'92s hope they didn\u8217\'92t base the algorithms on John\u8217\'92s erratic behavior. Otherwise, we\u8217\'92re doomed.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 John smirked, but the levity didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t last long. \u8220\'93Who\u8217\'92s the threat, then? Meera, if it\u8217\'92s not an insider, then what?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Meera hesitated, her eyes drifting to the faint star trails streaking the darkness outside. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Sometimes,\u8221\'94 she said slowly, \u8220\'93it\u8217\'92s not about who. It\u8217\'92s about what.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 That word hung in the air between them. What. John didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t need her to elaborate. He knew what she meant. Artificial systems, rogue constructs, black-box entities\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 they weren\u8217\'92t enemies you could negotiate with or out think. They just were. Relentless. Logical to a fault. And completely alien in their objectives.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You think the Federation lost control of something?\u8221\'94 he asked finally.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Lady Ava\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s silence was answer enough.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Ava looked between them, her usual sharp wit tempered now by a quiet unease. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You really know how to ruin the pre-mission vibes, don\u8217\'92t you?\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Ava stood, a smile drew accross her weathered cheeks as she rose, her exotic dress elegantly glid accross in her wake as she made her way to the exit expression hardening. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Whatever it is,\u8221\'94 he said, his voice firm now, \u8220\'93we deal with it tomorrow. Like we always do.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 But as she walked toward the hatch, Meera\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s parting words stopped his confidence for a moment. \u8220\'93Just remember, John,\u8221\'94 she said softly, \u8220\'93even if you don\u8217\'92t trust the system, trust your squad. The moment you start doubting them is the moment you lose.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 John nodded closing his eyes, his jaw Loosening. Trust. It was a currency he couldn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t afford to lose\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 not tomorrow, not ever}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
